          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of an
            %em enriched category
            is a generalization of the notion of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
          %p
            Very often, instead of merely having a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            to another, a category will have a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            of morphisms, or a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            of morphisms, or some other such thing. This suggests that we should take the definition of a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"}> locally small
            ) category and generalize it by replacing the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
            = succeed "," do
              %em hom-objects
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %p
            The category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            must be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo :
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ : hom(y,z) \otimes hom(x,y) \to hom(x,z)
          %p
            So, a
            %strong
              category enriched over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            (also called a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                category enriched in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            = succeed ")," do
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                \-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ob
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ob(C)
            of objects and, for each pair
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ob
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in ob(C)
            = succeed "\u2019" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi K
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(x,y) \in K .
          %p We then mimic the usual definition of a category.
          %p
            We may similarly define a
            %em
              functor enriched over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            and a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                natural transformation enriched over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
            of
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+V-enriched+categories"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                \-Cat
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                \-enriched adjunctions
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                \-enriched equivalences
          %p
            There is also an enriched notion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            called a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
            = succeed "-Cat)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %p
            More generally, we may allow
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            to be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategory"} multicategory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category"} double category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+double+category"} virtual double category
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Ordinarily, enriched categories are considered as
            %em enriched over
            or
            %em enriched in
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#InMonoidCat"} Enrichment in a monoidal category
          %p
            More generally, one may think of a monoidal category as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            with a single object (so that the monoidal product becomes
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal composition
            %em enrichment in a bicategory
            \. This is discussed in the section
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#InBicat"} Enrichment in a bicategory
          %p
            Enriched categories and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
            between them form themselves a category, the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+V-enriched+categories"} category of V-enriched categories
          %h3#InMonoidCat Enrichment in a monoidal category
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            with
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                tensor product
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo :
                        %mi V
                        %mo ×
                        %mi V
                        %mo →
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \otimes : V \times V \to V
            %li
              %p
                tensor unit
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Obj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \in Obj(V)
            %li
              %p
                associator
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mrow
                            %mi a
                            %mo ,
                            %mi b
                            %mo ,
                            %mi c
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi c
                        %mo →
                        %mi a
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi c
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_{a,b,c} : (a \otimes b)\otimes c \to a \otimes (b \otimes c)
            %li
              %p
                left unitor
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi I
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi a
                        %mo →
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_a : I \otimes a \to a
            %li
              %p
                right unitor
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi r
                          %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi a
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi I
                        %mo →
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r_a : a \otimes I \to a
          %p
            A (small)
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              \-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (or
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              \-enriched category
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong
                category enriched over/in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
